1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,001
The voice media library holds the audio your phone system plays:

2
00:00:05,001 --> 00:00:08,774
hold music for queues, and recorded prompts for phone menus.

3
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:12,661
This video shows why it exists, how to add and replace a clip,

4
00:00:12,661 --> 00:00:15,690
what the badges mean, and where a clip is used.

5
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:25,596
Callers hear audio while they wait, and when a phone menu asks them to choose.

6
00:00:25,596 --> 00:00:30,080
That audio has to sound the same for every caller, on every line.

7
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:35,052
Phone providers keep the files you send them, but they can lose them,

8
00:00:35,052 --> 00:00:39,330
and a copy kept only at one provider is gone when you change provider.

9
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:44,621
The voice media library keeps a master copy of every clip on your

10
00:00:44,621 --> 00:00:47,947
site, and sends a copy to your phone provider.

11
00:00:47,947 --> 00:00:51,720
If the provider loses its copy, it is sent a new one.

12
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:57,671
A clip is uploaded once, and then picked by name wherever it is needed:

13
00:00:57,671 --> 00:01:00,170
on a queue, or in a phone menu.

14
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:08,490
Open Interaction Center, Management, Voice Media.

15
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:10,463
The library is empty.

16
00:01:10,463 --> 00:01:12,510
Click Add Voice Media.

17
00:01:15,203 --> 00:01:19,518
Enter a Name that people will recognize, such as Main hold music, and

18
00:01:19,518 --> 00:01:24,063
an optional Description that says which business or line the clip is for.

19
00:01:24,598 --> 00:01:29,122
Under Audio, choose an M.P.3, wave, O.G.G.

20
00:01:29,122 --> 00:01:33,458
or web M file of up to twenty megabytes.

21
00:01:33,924 --> 00:01:34,944
Click Save.

22
00:01:34,944 --> 00:01:39,264
The platform keeps the file as the clip's master copy, and sends a

23
00:01:39,264 --> 00:01:41,244
copy to the phone provider.

24
00:01:41,712 --> 00:01:45,382
The clip is listed with its format and a Master copy badge, and

25
00:01:45,382 --> 00:01:46,659
when it was saved.

26
00:01:46,659 --> 00:01:50,542
If the phone provider does not accept the upload, the clip is still

27
00:01:50,542 --> 00:01:53,522
saved with its master copy, and you see a warning.

28
00:01:57,722 --> 00:02:01,016
Master copy means the platform holds the audio.

29
00:02:01,016 --> 00:02:05,553
The clip plays on any phone provider, and a provider that loses its

30
00:02:05,553 --> 00:02:09,842
copy is sent a new one automatically, within about ten minutes.

31
00:02:10,592 --> 00:02:16,212
Provider copy only marks a clip that was uploaded before the platform kept master copies.

32
00:02:16,212 --> 00:02:20,177
It plays at the provider it was uploaded to, but it cannot be

33
00:02:20,177 --> 00:02:22,662
checked or sent to another provider.

34
00:02:23,412 --> 00:02:26,447
No audio means the clip has no audio yet.

35
00:02:26,447 --> 00:02:31,162
A badge with the provider's name shows which providers hold a copy.

36
00:02:35,368 --> 00:02:37,417
Click Edit to open a clip.

37
00:02:37,417 --> 00:02:42,089
Uploading a new file under Audio replaces the old audio everywhere:

38
00:02:42,089 --> 00:02:47,658
the old master copy and every provider's copy are removed once the clip is saved.

39
00:02:48,287 --> 00:02:53,082
A clip marked Provider copy only is lost if you change phone provider,

40
00:02:53,082 --> 00:02:55,353
or if the provider deletes it.

41
00:02:55,353 --> 00:03:01,347
To protect it, open the clip, choose the original file again under Audio, and click Save.

42
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:06,367
Click Re-sync media on a clip to check that every enabled phone provider

43
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:10,256
still holds it, and to send it to any provider that does not.

44
00:03:10,256 --> 00:03:12,520
Use it after you change provider.

45
00:03:12,976 --> 00:03:15,355
You see a message for each provider:

46
00:03:15,355 --> 00:03:19,264
that it already held the clip, that it received a copy, or that

47
00:03:19,264 --> 00:03:20,850
it did not accept one.

48
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:24,136
The button appears only on clips with a master copy.

49
00:03:28,336 --> 00:03:33,716
On a queue, pick the clip as Hold music, on the While callers wait card.

50
00:03:34,466 --> 00:03:35,636
In an I.V.R.

51
00:03:35,636 --> 00:03:38,886
menu, pick it as the menu's Recorded prompt.

52
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:43,323
The first time a provider plays a clip it has no copy of,

53
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:45,781
it is sent one from the master copy.

54
00:03:45,781 --> 00:03:49,526
A caller may notice a short delay on that first call only.

55
00:03:50,276 --> 00:03:53,183
Your voicemail greeting is kept the same way:

56
00:03:53,183 --> 00:03:57,856
the platform holds the master copy, and sends it to whichever phone provider

57
00:03:57,856 --> 00:03:59,566
a caller reaches you on.

58
00:04:03,865 --> 00:04:06,612
Click Delete on a clip, and confirm.

59
00:04:06,612 --> 00:04:10,535
The master copy and every provider's copy are removed.

60
00:04:12,135 --> 00:04:16,665
Queues and phone menus that pointed at the clip fall back to their

61
00:04:16,665 --> 00:04:20,125
spoken text, or to silence, so update them first.

62
00:04:20,875 --> 00:04:25,857
When you move to another site, voice media entries travel in deployment plans,

63
00:04:25,857 --> 00:04:27,577
but the audio does not.

64
00:04:27,577 --> 00:04:32,262
Open each imported clip and upload its audio again; queues and menus that

65
00:04:32,262 --> 00:04:36,235
use it start playing the new audio as soon as it is uploaded.

66
00:04:40,435 --> 00:04:46,145
A support team uploads its hold music once, and every queue plays the same audio.

67
00:04:46,895 --> 00:04:51,648
A company records its menu prompts, one for each language, and picks them

68
00:04:51,648 --> 00:04:54,355
in the phone menus of its entry points.

69
00:04:55,105 --> 00:04:59,256
A business that moves to a new phone provider re-syncs its clips, and

70
00:04:59,256 --> 00:05:01,415
nothing has to be uploaded again.

71
00:05:02,165 --> 00:05:06,419
A team that updates its seasonal greeting uploads the new file to the

72
00:05:06,419 --> 00:05:10,445
same clip, and every queue and menu that uses it changes at once.

73
00:05:12,445 --> 00:05:16,832
Upload each clip once, keep its master copy on your site, and pick

74
00:05:16,832 --> 00:05:19,451
it by name on queues and phone menus.

75
00:05:19,451 --> 00:05:21,035
Thanks for watching.

